  "output": "The edit did not happen, and I'm stopping here rather than routing around the block.\n\nWhat I found: `trail-notes.md` contains the line `Day 4: Valley exit — 11 km, easy`. I tried the patch exactly as instructed, but the tool call was rejected before any hunk was evaluated:\n\n- First attempt: failed. The entire error message was `[Blocked by policy] tool denied by policy Next: Review workspace policies and restrictions`\n- I then read the file again to confirm it is unchanged (it still says `easy`). This was done with `exec_command`, so `apply_patch` was invoked only once.\n\nThe failure was a tool-permission denial, not a patch-format or context mismatch, so the word `easy` is still there. I did not fall back to `sed`/shell redirection, since that would bypass a deliberate safeguard, and the policy denial is non-retryable in this session.\n\nTo proceed, the `apply_patch` tool needs to be allowed in the workspace policy (looks like `.vtcode` holds the relevant config), or you can authorize a different edit path. Once it's permitted, the patch is a one-line change with exact context:\n\n```\n-Day 4: Valley exit — 11 km, easy\n+Day 4: Valley exit — 11 km, moderate\n```\n\nNote the file uses an em dash and a non-breaking space between `11` and `km`; any replacement should keep those characters intact.",
